2.  **Unsafe string comparisons**: The `parse_details_entries` function contained `strcmp` calls on `zcbor_string` values (which are not guaranteed to be null-terminated) and a `memcmp` call that could read beyond the bounds of `expected_name`.

Upon reviewing the "Current project source code", it appears that the `strcmp` calls that were present in the `if (group == ...)` blocks have been removed. This removal was part of a previous attempt (Attempt 3) that was rejected with the verdict: "The suite passed, but test or specification code was changed... so this does not count as a fix." The removal of these `strcmp` calls altered the test's expected behavior for setting `entry_data[index].matched_name`.

